tion and Prolonged QTc Interval of Uncertain Aetiology", "c3_l1_axis": {"mode": "flat", "case_id": "74", "max_l1": 6, "keep_leaves": false, "n_l1": 1, "n_l2": 0, "seed_base": 20260728}}, "branches": {"FLAT": {"id": "FLAT", "label": "Flat candidate pool (no L1 hierarchy)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "level_role": "family", "status": "live", "prior": 1.0, "posterior": 1.0, "danger": 0.0, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "classification_axis": "fixed_specialty", "representative_diseases": [], "askable_discriminators": [], "requestable_discriminators": [], "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "reopen_triggers": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.0, "interrupt_relevance": 0.0, "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0}}, "case_id": "74", "case_summary": "A 21-year-old woman with autism spectrum disorder (on risperidone) and intellectual disability was brought to the hospital after a witnessed collapse. She had no prior history of syncope, cardiac arrest, or known cardiovascular disease, and her family denied any illicit drug or alcohol use. While at a noisy auto mechanic shop, she became pale and lost consciousness; bystander ECG showed ventricular fibrillation. Return of spontaneous circulation was achieved after two defibrillations. On arrival, her blood pressure was 93/70 mmHg, pulse 86 bpm, and oxygen saturation 100% (bag–valve–mask). An intravenous amiodarone infusion (1 mg/min) and oral amiodarone 400 mg were administered. On examination she was comatose (GCS 3), with agonal respirations; cardiovascular examination was unremarkable. In the intensive care unit, her differential diagnosis included channelopathies, hypertrophic cardiomyopathy, and metabolic abnormalities. Laboratory tests showed normal chemistry panel and electrolytes. Initial electrocardiogram revealed sinus rhythm with interpolated premature ventricular complexes and a QTc of 380 ms, without any evidence of infarction, pre-excitation, or Brugada pattern. Transthoracic echocardiography demonstrated an ejection fraction of 45–50%, normal wall thickness, and no valvular abnormalities.", "frontier": ["FLAT"], "root": {"alarm_features": ["Coma", "Agonal respirations", "Ventricular fibrillation"], "confidence": 0.6, "excluded_candidates": ["Channelopathies: considered due to prolonged QTc interval, but further evaluation is needed", "Hypertrophic cardiomyopathy: considered due to reduced ejection fraction, but normal wall thickness on echocardiography makes it less likely", "Metabolic abnormalities: considered due to coma and agonal respirations, but normal chemistry panel and electrolytes make it less likely"], "label": "Acute Comatose State with Ventricular Fibrillation and Prolonged QTc Interval of Uncertain Aetiology", "salient_findings": ["Ventricular fibrillation", "Prolonged QTc interval", "Coma", "Agonal respirations", "EF of 45-50%", "Normal wall thickness on echocardiography"], "severity": "unspecified", "supporting_facts": ["Witnessed collapse with ventricular fibrillation", "Comatose state with agonal respirations", "Prolonged QTc interval of 380 ms", "Normal chemistry panel and electrolytes"], "time_course": "acute"}, "static_evidence_items": [{"branch_links": {}, "content": "Demographics: 21-year-old woman with autism spectrum disorder and intellectual disability", "id": "E1", "independent": true, "kind": "direct", "metadata": {"extractor": "diagnosisarena_vignette_parser_freeze_v2"}, "source_ids": []}, {"branch_links": {}, "content": "Medication: risperidone", "id": "E2", "independent": true, "kind": "direct", "metadata": {"extractor": "diagnosisarena_vignette_parser_freeze_v2"}, "source_ids": []}, {"branch_links": {}, "content": "Chief complaint: witnessed collapse", "id": "E3", "independent": true, "kind": "direct", "metadata": {"extractor": "diagnosisarena_vignette_parser_freeze_v2"}, "source_ids": []}, {"branch_links": {}, "content": "No prior histo